From f290efb6c42ae7eadb70330b64b2c2821b8d8c84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:07:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-101: the events list as clear as WPF's; the caret
 into the handler's body (0.101.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20260930: "先讓使用者可以和 wpf 改 code 一樣方便有效率 ... 事件可以像 wpf 讓使用者
看起來條理分明".
- The events list: "元件事件（C++）" and "網頁事件（JS）", both the same two columns
  (the event | its function), the names where the property names start; the web
  list's paragraph is its heading's tooltip; an empty handler box is empty (its
  default name was a grey placeholder that looked like a value -- now it shows
  while you are in the box); "另外還有 N 個（見下面）" is "+N" (the listeners are
  in the code list since 0.99).
- WPF "navigates to the existing handler" with the caret in it: a double-click
  on a set event opens its code with the caret on the first statement of the body
  (cppstub.bodyStart: the first '{' within 30 lines, comments and strings masked;
  an empty body = just after its brace), not on the function's name. A new
  handler already opened with its placeholder selected inside the body.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 161, smoke 186, panels, real VS Code 159): lib
(bodyStart: the first statement, an empty body, a brace in a comment on the
signature line ignored, no brace); real VS Code (sbCloseProgram OnClick opens
W906_Main_CloseProgramOp with the caret inside its body).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
